dichromat: Color Schemes for Dichromats

Collapse red-green or green-blue distinctions to simulate the effects of
different types of color-blindness based on the work of Françoise Viénot
and co-authors, especially &lt;<a href="https://doi.org/10.1038%2F376127a0"
target="_top">doi:10.1038/376127a0</a>&gt; and &lt;<a
href="https://doi.org/10.1364%2Fjosaa.14.002647"
target="_top">doi:10.1364/josaa.14.002647</a>&gt;. More recent functions
for simulating color vision deficiency are provided in the 'colorspace'
package.


